; Post-repair audit after round three found ambiguous synset-only lookup.
import "../form/form-stdlib/core.fk"
import "review-panel.fk"
import "review-ask.fk"

(ra-review
  "cognition/form-neutral-word-field-locales.fk"
  "Post-repair adversarial verification only; do not edit any file. Read cognition/form-neutral-word-field-locales.fk, cognition/tests/form-neutral-word-field-locales-band.fk, and observe/form-neutral-word-field-locales-live.fk. Round three returned REVISE because first-synset-match was ambiguous for duplicated synsets, corpus source refs did not uniquely identify the selected concept row, only seven surfaces had independent literal witnesses, and invalid public inputs could open the corpus before refusal. Verify those exact repairs. Each body row reference must now carry catalog, synset, and stable neutral concept ID; fwfl-body-key-valid? must verify the concept ID resolves to the same synset in the loaded substrate; generation must use that ID directly, never scan for a first synset or use an English headword. The canonical 7x13 grid must hash in Form to 5869acd3021a7b8b8bb39d319ab456cd00a6941f3c8a0357c50a6a4b7fa58170, and the fresh band must return 16777215. Wrong tags, negative and out-of-range IDs, invalid locales, and empty reverse queries must refuse before fwfl-runtime opens the corpus. Confirm 91 exact surfaces, 91 identity roundtrips, 19 runtime corpus realizations, 72 local character-complete bridges split 52 composite/20 single, source counts 61/19/11, nine-field records, 91 speaker-unreviewed/0 reviewed, exact code-point matching without normalization, and zero learned or productive morphology. Do not call indexed lookup generation from semantic geometry; the file must retain the irreducible lexical-memory boundary. Return PASS AS A BOUNDED NEUTRAL-SYMBOL-FIRST REALIZATION SEED, REVISE, or BLOCK with the smallest executable finding. Empty or unavailable doors are absence, never votes.")
